    # v395 (21/10/2026) -- THE PSIBIT: the mechanics on the fractalized One and the lossless reading; the numbers are READ from the psibit_v395 record (which computes them in this run and checks them against the kernel of the run itself)
    # and from the cunhagens_v395 and kh_n1_cobertura_v395 records. Nothing here moves the gate.
    _pb395 = core.get("psibit_v395") or {}
    _pv395 = _pb395.get("values") or {}
    _un395 = _pb395.get("unconditional") or {}
    _cd395 = _pb395.get("conditional_psion_face") or {}
    _cg395 = core.get("cunhagens_v395") or {}
    _kh395 = core.get("kh_n1_cobertura_v395") or {}
    _el395 = core.get("external_ladder") or {}
    _kf395 = core.get("kernel_formalization") or {}
    _cv395 = ((core.get("kernel_formalization") or {}).get("axiom_coverage_v392")) or {}
    _i395 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _f395 = lambda x_, nd_=12: ("%.*f" % (nd_, x_)) if isinstance(x_, float) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _e395 = lambda x_: ("%.1e" % x_) if isinstance(x_, float) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _d395 = (_pv395.get("collapse_diagonal") or [None, None])
    s.append(r"\section*{The psibit: the mechanics on the fractalized One and the lossless reading}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The psibit: the mechanics on the fractalized One and the lossless reading}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{This round the record did NOT seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if not (_pb395.get("all_verified") is True) else r"")
             + r"\textbf{What enters.} One new kernel module, \texttt{TGLExt/Psibit} (the name is the operator's: ``I prefer it to be psibit''), with " + _i395(_V395_PSIBIT_CONTRACT.get("n_flags")) + r" flags, named declarations only; the record \texttt{psibit\_v395}, called at the point of the run where the One is fractalized "
             r"(the fractal dephasing principle); and the " + _i395(len(_V395_VERBATINS2)) + r" operator inscriptions of 21 Oct, embedded by sha256 (record \texttt{cunhagens\_v395}). The kernel ladder reads " + _i395(_el395.get("n_theorems_clean")) + r" of " + _i395(_el395.get("n_theorems_expected"))
             + r"; the \texttt{axiom\_report} coverage over the whole closure reads " + _i395(_cv395.get("decl")) + r" constants and " + _i395(_cv395.get("thm")) + r" theorems, none outside the trio $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$. "
             r"The stone went through independent review in two rounds (the second approved it) and is checked at every run against the embedded body, by sha256. The v394 stone with a provisional name, \texttt{TheBinaryReadingAtTheFixedPoint}, stays as a record and is cited by the conjunction; its flag "
             + (r"remains true" if _kf395.get("ext_bin394_0001") is True else r"does NOT remain true") + r".")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The mechanics on the orbit of the One.} At $\theta_M=\arcsin\sqrt{\beta}$, with $\beta=\alpha\sqrt{e}$ computed in this run ($\beta=" + _f395(_pv395.get("beta"), 15) + r"$; $\theta_M=" + _f395(_pv395.get("theta_M_rad"), 9) + r"$ rad $=" + _f395(_pv395.get("theta_M_deg"), 4)
             + r"^\circ$), the orbit of the One through the S-matrix is $v(\theta)=(\cos\theta,-\sin\theta)$ and the fractalization $F_\theta(1)=\rho_{\mathrm{out}}(\theta)=|v\rangle\langle v|$ is the rank-one projector "
             r"$\begin{pmatrix}c^2&-cs\\-sc&s^2\end{pmatrix}$, with $c^2=" + _f395(_d395[0], 9) + r"$, $-cs=" + _f395(_pv395.get("coherence"), 9) + r"$, $s^2=" + _f395(_d395[1], 9) + r"$. "
             r"The \emph{psibit code} is the weight $c^2$ plus the pair of signs $(\operatorname{sign}L,\operatorname{sign}\partial L)$, with $L=\cos\theta$ (the transmission) and $\partial L=-\sin\theta$ (the reflection, the derivative of the transmission): here $(" + _i395(_pv395.get("code_word")) + r"," + _i395(_pv395.get("code_verb"))
             + r")$, and the parity, the product of the signs, is $" + _i395(_pv395.get("parity")) + r"$. The decoder $(w,a,b)\mapsto(a\sqrt{w},\,b\sqrt{1-w})$ returns the amplitude with residual $" + _e395(_pv395.get("decode_residual"))
             + r"$ (bound $10^{-12}$): reading the pair loses nothing. The Verb is half the derivative of the Name, $\rho_{01}=\tfrac12\,\mathrm{d}(\cos^2\theta)/\mathrm{d}\theta$ (finite-difference residual $" + _e395(_pv395.get("verb_derivative_residual")) + r"$).")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The collapse.} The collapse $D_\infty$ (the diagonal) of $\rho(\theta)$ and of $\rho(-\theta)$ is the same (difference $" + _e395(_pv395.get("collapse_diag_difference")) + r"$) and the coherences are opposite ($" + _f395(_pv395.get("coherence"), 9) + r"$ and $" + _f395(_pv395.get("coherence_neg_theta"), 9)
             + r"$): the collapse loses exactly the parity, one bit, and the full reading remembers it. The separant (the reading of the pair, injective) and the separator (the collapse, many-to-one) sit in the same object. "
             r"At equal weights ($\theta=\pi/4+k\pi/2$) the collapse is $\tfrac12 I$ and the Shannon entropy of the outcomes is $\ln 2=" + _f395(_pv395.get("ln2"), 12) + r"$ (residual $" + _e395(_pv395.get("entropy_balanced_residual")) + r"$); at $\theta_M$ it reads $" + _f395(_pv395.get("entropy_at_theta_M"), 6)
             + r"$, below $\ln 2$, and no angle exceeds it. What is lost is a variable (which one), not a quantity of information stated in general.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{What the kernel proves and what is reading.} The conjunction \texttt{psibit\_is\_the\_mode\_of\_the\_reader} is \emph{unconditional} (no certificate is a hypothesis): " + (r"it is in the kernel of this run, inside the trio" if _un395.get("in_kernel") is True else r"it was NOT read in the kernel of this run")
             + r". The bijection is one of \emph{sets}, between the unit circle and the code book, with an explicit decoder; it is not a Hilbert-space isomorphism, and it is not all of quantum mechanics. "
             r"The psion face, \texttt{the\_psion\_face\_of\_the\_psibit}, is a separate and \emph{conditional} theorem: it holds for every Fock certificate of the light, and the kernel exhibits no inhabitant of the certificate, so the statement does not show that the psion exists. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} the theorems and the computation; \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]} psibit $=$ psion $=$ the reader's mode is the operator's reading (21 Oct 2026), and no lemma links the psion to the code; \textsf{[CONDITIONAL]} the psion face. The records \texttt{cunhagens\_v395} "
             + (r"and \texttt{kh\_n1\_cobertura\_v395} sealed in this run." if (_cg395.get("all_verified") is True and _kh395.get("all_verified") is True) else r"and \texttt{kh\_n1\_cobertura\_v395} did NOT both seal in this run."))
    s.append(r"\textbf{Limits.} The parity is the product $\operatorname{sign}L\cdot\operatorname{sign}\partial L$ (formula, claims 3 and 4 and code of the ACOM Mirror patent); the table of the same patent reads it from the second sign, and which reading is canonical is the operator's decision \textsf{[LEGAL]}. "
             r"The entropy equals $\ln 2$ only at equal weights; the computation is numerical, in double precision: it checks the theorems and does not prove them, the kernel does. Kernel validity is not creditation, and the gate does not move.")
